---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro'
---
<DocsLayout title="Options">
  <h1>Options</h1>
  <p class="lead">All options are optional. Pass them as the second argument to <code>new Slider(target, options)</code>.</p>

  <h2>Layout</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>items</code></td><td>number</td><td><code>1</code></td><td>Number of slides visible at once.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>gutter</code></td><td>number</td><td><code>0</code></td><td>Gap in px between slides.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>edgePadding</code></td><td>number</td><td><code>0</code></td><td>Peek px from each side, revealing adjacent slides.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>fixedWidth</code></td><td>number | false</td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Fixed px width per slide instead of fluid columns.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>autoWidth</code></td><td>boolean</td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Each slide keeps its own intrinsic width.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>viewportMax</code></td><td>number | false</td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Max viewport width, used with <code>fixedWidth</code> to compute how many clones a loop needs.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>center</code></td><td>boolean</td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Centre the active slide in the viewport.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>axis</code></td><td><code>'horizontal' | 'vertical'</code></td><td><code>'horizontal'</code></td><td>Scroll direction. Vertical requires a fixed container height.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>container</code></td><td>string | HTMLElement</td><td><code>'.slider'</code></td><td>Fallback element when no target is passed to <code>new Slider()</code>. The first argument takes precedence.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>mode</code></td><td><code>'carousel'</code></td><td><code>'carousel'</code></td><td>Only carousel mode exists.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Navigation</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>loop</code></td><td>boolean</td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Infinite circular navigation. Clones boundary slides.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>rewind</code></td><td>boolean</td><td><code>false</code></td><td>At the last slide Next jumps back to the first (and vice-versa). Implies <code>loop:false</code>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>slideBy</code></td><td>number | <code>'page'</code></td><td><code>1</code></td><td>Slides advanced per arrow click. <code>'page'</code> equals <code>items</code>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>startIndex</code></td><td>number</td><td><code>0</code></td><td>0-based index of the initial slide.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>speed</code></td><td>number</td><td><code>300</code></td><td>Transition duration in ms.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>arrowKeys</code></td><td>boolean</td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Navigate with keyboard ← → arrow keys.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>preventActionWhenRunning</code></td><td>boolean</td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Ignore nav input while a transition is in progress.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Touch & drag</h2>
  <p>Want lerped drag with inertia, trackpad scroll and presets instead? Turn these off and use the <a href="/docs/plugins/smooth">smooth plugin</a>: <code>touch: false, mouseDrag: false, plugins: [smooth()]</code>.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>touch</code></td><td>boolean</td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Enable touch swipe navigation.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>mouseDrag</code></td><td>boolean</td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Enable click-and-drag on desktop.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>peek</code></td><td>string</td><td><code>''</code></td><td>Keeps this width free on the right so the next card shows, e.g. <code>'20%'</code>. It makes the outer narrower, sets <code>overflow: 'visible'</code> and clips the slider's wrapper so the page doesn't scroll sideways (undone on <code>destroy()</code>). For <code>items: 1</code> sliders.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>overflow</code></td><td>'hidden' | 'visible'</td><td><code>'hidden'</code></td><td><code>'visible'</code> shows neighbouring cards outside the slider (peek / centered layouts). Also narrow <code>.sliderkit__outer</code> (e.g. <code>width: 80%</code>) and put <code>overflow: hidden</code> on a wrapper so the page does not scroll sideways.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>swipeAngle</code></td><td>number | false</td><td><code>15</code></td><td>Max degrees from the axis direction to register as a swipe. <code>false</code> disables angle filtering.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>preventScrollOnTouch</code></td><td><code>'auto' | 'force' | false</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Whether to call <code>preventDefault()</code> on touch events to block page scroll.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Behaviour</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>autoHeight</code></td><td>boolean</td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Animate container height to match each slide's natural height on transition.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>freezable</code></td><td>boolean</td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Auto-freeze (disable) when all slides fit on one page.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>lazyload</code></td><td>boolean</td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Wait for images to load before the first transform.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Responsive</h2>
  <p>Pass a <code>responsive</code> map to override any option at specific window widths. Keys are min-width breakpoints in px.</p>
  <pre><code>new Slider('#my-slider', {"{"}
  items: 1,
  gutter: 8,
  responsive: {"{"}
    640:  {"{"} items: 2, gutter: 16 {"}"},
    960:  {"{"} items: 3, gutter: 20 {"}"},
    1280: {"{"} items: 4, gutter: 24 {"}"},
  {"}"},
{"}"})</code></pre>
  <h3>What you can set inside <code>responsive</code></h3>
  <p>Not every option reacts to the window width. Anything not marked <strong>Yes</strong> is ignored inside <code>responsive</code> (no error, it just does nothing), so check this table before relying on it.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Inside <code>responsive</code></th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>items</code>, <code>slideBy</code></td><td><strong>Yes</strong></td><td>Updated every time a breakpoint is crossed.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>speed</code>, <code>center</code>, <code>autoHeight</code>, <code>fixedWidth</code></td><td><strong>Yes</strong></td><td>Updated every time a breakpoint is crossed.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>touch</code>, <code>mouseDrag</code>, <code>arrowKeys</code></td><td><strong>Yes</strong></td><td>Updated every time a breakpoint is crossed.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>loop</code>, <code>rewind</code></td><td><strong>Yes</strong>, with limits</td><td>Clones are added or removed and you stay on the same card. Ignored with <code>edgePadding</code>, <code>fixedWidth</code>, <code>autoWidth</code> and effect or WebGL plugins. See below.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>gutter</code>, <code>edgePadding</code></td><td><strong>Yes</strong>, layout only</td><td>The sizes change, but the values used for drag maths and for the number of loop clones are read once. Keep them similar across breakpoints.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>startIndex</code>, <code>overflow</code>, <code>peek</code></td><td>At load only</td><td>Uses the breakpoint that matches when the slider is created. Resizing afterwards does not change them.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>plugins</code></td><td>No</td><td>Installed once at creation. See the recipes below.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>autoWidth</code>, <code>axis</code>, <code>viewportMax</code>, <code>freezable</code>, <code>lazyload</code></td><td>No</td><td>Base options only, read once.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>swipeAngle</code>, <code>preventScrollOnTouch</code>, <code>preventActionWhenRunning</code></td><td>No</td><td>Base options only, read once.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>container</code>, <code>mode</code>, <code>onInit</code></td><td>No</td><td>Base options only.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Effects and WebGL</td><td>No</td><td>They control the slide styles for the whole life of the slider. Choose them at load.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>The slider recalculates its layout and pagination on each resize that crosses a breakpoint.</p>

  <h3><code>loop</code> and <code>rewind</code> per breakpoint</h3>
  <p>Both can go inside <code>responsive</code>. When the window crosses the breakpoint the slider adds or removes its clones and stays on the same card, with no animation. <code>rewind: true</code> still turns the loop off, only at the widths where it is active.</p>
  <pre><code>{`new Slider('#my-slider', {
  items: 1, loop: true,
  responsive: { 1024: { items: 3, loop: false } },
})`}</code></pre>
  <p>If the current card does not exist without the loop (for example card 6 when 3 cards are visible), the slider moves to the last valid position and emits <code>indexChanged</code>. It is ignored, and the slider keeps its current loop, when it uses <code>edgePadding</code> or <code>fixedWidth</code>, or when an effect plugin or WebGL is installed (a warning is logged).</p>

  <h3>What to do when it can't change</h3>
  <p>The most common cases from the table above:</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Why</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>plugins</code></td><td>Plugins are installed once.</td><td>Hide them with CSS, choose them at load, or recreate the slider.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>overflow</code>, <code>peek</code></td><td>Applied when the slider is created.</td><td>Recreate the slider, or set the CSS yourself with a media query.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Effects and WebGL</td><td>They control the slide styles for the whole life of the slider.</td><td>Choose them at load.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>Recipes</h3>
  <p><strong>Arrows only on desktop.</strong> Hide them with CSS. It reacts to every resize and needs no JavaScript. <code>display: none</code> also removes them from the tab order.</p>
  <pre><code>{`new Slider('#my-slider', { items: 1, plugins: [arrows()] })

@media (max-width: 1023px) {
  .sliderkit__arrows { display: none; }
}`}</code></pre>
  <p>If you passed <code>container</code> to <code>arrows()</code>, hide that container instead.</p>

  <p><strong>A plugin only above a certain width, decided at load.</strong> It does not react if the window is resized afterwards.</p>
  <pre><code>{`const plugins = [arrows()]
if (window.innerWidth >= 960) {
  plugins.push(progress({ container: '#my-progress' }))
}

new Slider('#my-slider', { plugins })`}</code></pre>

  <p><strong>Different plugins per width, also on resize.</strong> Recreate the slider when the width crosses the breakpoint. <code>matchMedia</code> fires only when it crosses, not on every pixel, and the plugins must be created again inside the function. The new slider starts at the first slide.</p>
  <pre><code>{`const mq = matchMedia('(min-width: 1024px)')
const make = () => new Slider('#my-slider', {
  items: mq.matches ? 3 : 1,
  plugins: mq.matches ? [arrows()] : [pagination()],
})

let slider = make()
mq.addEventListener('change', () => { slider.destroy(); slider = make() })`}</code></pre>

  <p><strong>Run your own code when a breakpoint is crossed.</strong> The slider emits an event, only when it has a <code>responsive</code> map. Call your function once after creating the slider as well, because the event does not fire at load.</p>
  <pre><code>{`slider.on('newBreakpointEnd', () => {
  document.querySelector('.sliderkit__arrows').hidden = window.innerWidth < 1024
})`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Callbacks & plugins</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>onInit</code></td><td>function | false</td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Called once after the slider is fully initialised. Receives a <a href="/docs/events"><code>SliderInfo</code></a> object.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>plugins</code></td><td>SliderPlugin[]</td><td><code>[]</code></td><td>Array of plugin instances. See <a href="/docs/plugins">Plugins</a>.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</DocsLayout>
